course: dictionary
lesson: 7919
title: Razor-sharp words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A razor is a tool with a very sharp blade, used to shave hair off the face, legs or head. Because its blade cuts so easily, razors are for grown-ups only.
explain: Context gives you the clues. «Children never use or play with grown-ups' razors, because the blades are extremely sharp.» The words extremely sharp tell you why children must keep away from them.
explain: Razor can also be part of a describing word, razor-sharp. «Glass breaks with smooth, razor-sharp edges» means the edges are extremely sharp. A razor-sharp mind is very quick and clever. Swap in extremely sharp to check that your meaning makes sense.
fact: A razor is a tool with a very sharp blade, used for shaving hair.
fact: An electric razor is a small machine that shaves hair with moving blades.
fact: «Razor-sharp» means extremely sharp, or a very quick, clever mind.
fact: «Razor blade» and «electric razor» are common phrases.
fact: Razors, craft knives and box cutters are for grown-ups only, because their blades slip easily.
exercise: «Children never use or play with grown-ups' razors, because the blades are extremely sharp.» Why must children never play with razors? | *Because razors are only for cooking | Because razors are heavy and slow | Because razors are made of wood | Because the blades are extremely sharp
exercise: «Glass breaks with smooth, razor-sharp edges.» What does razor-sharp mean here? | *Extremely sharp | Covered in paint | Dull and bumpy | Soft and warm
exercise: What is an electric razor? | *A small machine that shaves hair with moving blades | A kind of glass that cannot break | A bowl for hot soup | A tool for cutting paper
test: Which of these is a tool with a very sharp blade for shaving hair? | A balloon | A kettle | A ruler | *A razor
test: Nadia says someone has a razor-sharp mind. What does this mean? | They have a sharp blade in their head | They are always cold | *They are very quick and clever | They shave their hair every day
exam: Who should use razors and box cutters, according to the sentences? | Toddlers, to learn | Children who are very careful | Anyone who is bored | *Grown-ups only
